# Backend MCP

Governor for `backend/src/mcp`. Executor: `.cursor/skills/backend/backend-mcp/SKILL.md`.

## Hard rules

- Tools call the same TypeScript **services** as HTTP handlers — **no HTTP loopback**.
- One MCP tool per domain (`youtube`, `trends`, `instagram`, `twitter`, `gsearch`, `transcription`, `viral_clipper`, `tightening`). New functions are new **ops**, not new tools.
- Top-level args are only `{ op, layer?, input }`. Reuse API Zod `*_REQUEST_SCHEMA` as `input` — do not fork parallel MCP schemas.
- Default `layer` is `intel` when that overlay exists, else `raw`. Invalid combo **fails** — no silent fallback. Do not invent a fake intel layer.
- Wrap handlers with `ok` / `fail` from `tool-result.ts` (via `registerDomainTool`).
- Keep `MCP_TOOL_COUNT` equal to registered **domain** tools.
- Tool **description** must list ops, valid layers, and required input keys (JSON Schema cannot vary `input` per op).
- Always register every domain tool — do not skip mounts/tools based on `VERCEL`.
- New HTTP base paths go through `ENDPOINTS` + `routes.ts` (platform skill) — don’t hardcode mounts only in the MCP router.
- Lead-gen (Maps / Facebook / LinkedIn) stays HTTP-only unless product asks otherwise.
